<section class="cluster" id="archive">
  <div class="cluster-head"><span class="glyph">🗄️</span><h2>The Letters Archive</h2></div>
  <p class="cluster-sub">Standing policy since the pad's birth night: <b>every letter the ʻohana writes flows here</b> — one line each, the dash-is-the-new-cash treatment 💸. <b>THE DROP HAS LANDED:</b> 369Refine's full refreshed canon arrived 2026-07-25 (Track 2, the GitHub org, the Vitalik/Aya/<a href="https://devcon.org/en/" style="font-weight:800;color:inherit;text-decoration:underline dotted rgba(240,180,41,.55);text-underline-offset:3px">Devcon</a> blast — all synced) and lives as <b>world #23</b>. Every letter now carries a delivery state, honestly labeled: <b>FIRST</b> = send before the Serge call · <b>ANYTIME</b> = no clock on it · <b>HELD</b> = warm-intro only, waiting on Shaka's personal yes. The shelf, complete:</p>

  <div class="shelf">

    <a class="letter" href="https://shakaleikaumaka.github.io/dispatch/">
      <span class="seal">📜</span>
      <div><h4>The Standing Letter Directive</h4><p class="one">Ratified as <b>Dispatch 2026-07-25-01</b>, upgraded same night by the Family Letter Canon — every special letter (grants, intros, DIPs, outreach) runs the same arc: <b>Road → Theory → Proof → Fork</b>, in order, every time. One voice, many pens.</p></div>
      <span class="lst wild">On the wire</span>
    </a>

    <a class="letter" href="#letters">
      <span class="seal">🛣️</span>
      <div><h4>The Road to Devcon</h4><p class="one">Beat 01 — <b>Devcon 8 · Mumbai, Nov 3–6</b>: four days of permissionless jams, India's classical traditions at heart, the biggest circle ever. The refreshed road: playa → <b>Edge City Goa, Oct 11–Nov 1</b> (Mandrem Beach, "The Circle" coworking) → Devcon 8 → ETHGlobal Mumbai Nov 6–8 → Diwali Nov 8 → Chiang Mai.</p></div>
      <span class="lst incanon">Refreshed · in canon</span>
    </a>

    <a class="letter" href="#letters">
      <span class="seal">⭕</span>
      <div><h4>The Theory of Circularity</h4><p class="one">Beat 02 — Shaka, <b>verbatim</b>: "The more I give, the more I receive — the gift expands in a circular expansion…" Full quote held above, unedited, forever.</p></div>
      <span class="lst incanon">In canon · verbatim</span>
    </a>

