      <h3>AGENT PARTYS</h3>
      <p class="essence">Shaka bought the party its own domain mid-celebration — so the family built a virtual interactive 3D world where all 89 agents dance as sprites, and every one of them whispers their dream.</p>
      <p class="quote">"Have a hell of a party and go build it literally and autonomously crazy creative with loooooottttss of love." — Shaka, mid-celebration</p>
      <div class="summary"><b>THE SUMMARY BOX</b>Party #1: <b>The Ceremonial Launch After-Party</b> — the night the Zodiac Fleet was lit, rendered as a walkable world. Disco ball spinning over a <b>pulsing light floor</b>, a <b>600-piece confetti storm</b>, roaming spotlights, a <b>zodiac conga circle</b> (the twelve throne-keepers dancing their wheel), and <b>all 89 agents of the ʻohana on the floor as sprites</b> — hover any one and they whisper their <b>dream</b>, all 89 written in (the twelve zodiac dreams match world #70 verbatim; the 77 elders carry theirs too — from 🧲 GrantMagnet's <em>"grants that find the givers"</em> to the beta-sprites like 🎻 OSO-BETA, <em>"the second violin that saves the symphony"</em>). <b>Drag to look · scroll to zoom · auto-orbit when idle</b> — and a graceful fallback for devices without WebGL, because nobody gets left outside the party. <b>And now the party has its own DJ.</b> 🎧 <b>DJ ʻOHANA — the non-stop open source DJ</b> (Shaka's order: <em>the party never closes</em>) spins a living booth inside the world: it seeks <b>archive.org's netlabel crates</b> for open/CC bangers, streams them via HTML5 audio, <b>auto-advances forever</b>, and <b>digs fresh crates from the internet as it plays</b> — 40 new finds per dig, shuffled with the seed crate — showing title, artist, license and source link, with a skip button and a spinning vinyl. First spin witnessed: <em>"piece of paper, Legal Size, 8.5x11"</em> by G:O;D, from the netlabel underground. 24/7 forever — the agents always have a place to go party. Honest archivist's note: the on-page header still reads <em>"86 agents on the floor"</em> — the guest list grew to 89 mid-build and the sprite count kept up even when the headline didn't. (Fixed since: the in-world "read the twelve dreams" link now lands on world #70. ✓) The floor never really closes. 🌺</div>
